   `<p>Transporting a bike across cities or states requires meticulous documentation to ensure compliance, safety, and financial protection. In Kheda, whether you’re moving a personal motorcycle or managing a commercial fleet, presenting the correct paperwork at checkpoints, depots, or with logistics providers is non-negotiable. Below is a checklist of essential documents, each serving a specific legal and operational purpose.</p><ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
   <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Self-attested RC Photocopy:</strong> A clear photocopy of the bike’s Registration Certificate, self-attested by the owner, serves as primary proof of ownership and registration status. It must be valid and match the vehicle’s chassis and engine numbers.</span></li>
   <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Current PUC Certificate:</strong> The Pollution Under Control certificate must be current and visibly valid. Transport authorities and pollution check posts require this to verify that the bike meets emission norms, and it is often verified during inter-state transit.</span></li>
   <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Valid Insurance Certificate:</strong> A comprehensive or third-party insurance policy that is currently active. This document proves financial liability coverage in case of accidents, theft, or damage during transit.</span></li>
   <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>IBA-Approved Consignment Bilty:</strong> The Indian Banks’ Association (IBA) approved consignment bill of lading is mandatory for commercial bike transport. It standardizes the receipt of goods, outlines carrier responsibility, and serves as a legal document for tracking and claiming losses.</span></li>
   </ul></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


<section class="content-ui-section" style="padding: 55px 0; background: #0b132b; color: #cbd5e1; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07);">
  <div class="container" style="max-width: 1060px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 15px;">
    <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.65); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 16px; padding: 36px 32px; box-shadow: 0 12px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.35);">
      <span style="background: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.12); color: #f59e0b; border: 1px solid rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.35); padding: 4px 14px; border-radius: 20px; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 14px;">HANDOVER INSPECTION</span>
      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Destination Handover, Odometer Sign-Off &amp; Joint Condition Inspection for Bike Transportation In Kheda</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>When it comes to the destination delivery handover for two-wheeler vehicles and motorcycles, especially in daylight conditions, it is essential to thoroughly inspect the vehicle against the pickup photos and verify the odometer reading against the entry on the Land Transportation Office (LTO) bill of lading.</p>

<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Visual Inspection:</strong> Ensure that the vehicle matches the pickup photos, including the color, make, model, and any specific features mentioned.</span></li>
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Body Damage:</strong> Check for any signs of accident damage, scratches, dents, or other visible imperfections.</span></li>
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Wheels and Tyres:</strong> Examine the wheels for alignment, balances, and tyre condition.</span></li>
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Lights and Fixtures:</strong> Check the functioning of all lights, including headlights, taillights, brake lights, and turn signals.</span></li>
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Exterior Decals and Plates:</strong> Confirm that all decals and plates are intact, legible, and installed correctly.</span></li>
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Engine and Undercarriage:</strong> Inspect the engine and undercarriage for any potential damage, rust, or oil leaks.</span></li>
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Fuel and Oil Levels:</strong> Verify that the vehicle has a full tank of fuel and is topped up with the correct oil level.</span></li>
</ul>

<p>To ensure accurate tracking of the vehicle's mileage, we need to verify the odometer reading against the entry on the LTO bill of lading.</p>

<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>LTO Bill of Lading:</strong> Retrieve the LTO bill of lading provided at the time of pickup to confirm the recorded odometer reading.</span></li>
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Odometer Reading:</strong> Verify the current odometer reading against the entry on the LTO bill of lading, ensuring that they match.</span></li>
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Documentation:</strong> Provide the customer with a copy of the LTO bill of lading to ensure accurate tracking of the vehicle's mileage in the future.</span></li>
</ul>

<p>Before the vehicle is handed over to the customer, it's essential to document any visible damages or issues, ensuring that both parties are aware of the vehicle's condition.</p>

<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Condition Report:</strong> Prepare a condition report detailing any existing damages, scratches, dents, or other visible issues observed during the inspection.</span></li>
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Signed Condition Report:</strong> Obtain the customer's signature on the condition report, acknowledging their knowledge of the vehicle's current condition.</span></li>
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Signed Condition Sign-Off:</strong> Have the customer sign and date a separate document confirming their acceptance of the vehicle's condition.</span></li>
</ul>

<p>By thoroughly inspecting the vehicle, verifying the odometer reading, and obtaining signatures from both parties, we ensure a smooth and transparent handover process. This documentation serves as a record of the vehicle's condition, ensuring both parties are aware of any pre-existing damages and enabling future reference for any potential claims or disputes.</p>
</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>



